usage: fixfirst [-h] [--store STORE]
                {init,list,interactive,serve,mcp,scan,import,show,run,mark-fixed,accept-baseline,report,export,configure,stop,resume,delete,graph,ask,knowledge,demo,dataset,evaluate,historical}
                ...

FixFirst: local, evidence-based Python troubleshooting

positional arguments:
  {init,list,interactive,serve,mcp,scan,import,show,run,mark-fixed,accept-baseline,report,export,configure,stop,resume,delete,graph,ask,knowledge,demo,dataset,evaluate,historical}
    init                create a session (does not run the project)
    list                list sessions
    interactive         terminal menu, no commands to remember
    serve               open the local web interface
    mcp                 serve FixFirst to coding agents over MCP (stdio)
    scan                run checks (pytest imports project code)
    import              import an existing log
    show                show the current state
    run                 run a check action from the plan
    mark-fixed          record a manual change and wait for verification
    accept-baseline     accept the changed tests and test settings as the new
                        baseline
    report              write the HTML and JSON report
    export              write a redacted report for sharing
    configure           change the goal or the interpreter
    stop                stop the session
    resume              resume the session
    delete              delete a session's local records
    graph               export the session's evidence graph
    ask                 ask why an action is advised, what the cause is, what
                        is unverified
    knowledge           export the domain knowledge graph and rule base
    demo                build and run an owned demo project (never your code)
    dataset             generate a labelled dataset by real execution
    evaluate            run the experiments on a dataset
    historical          replay sourced upstream regressions offline

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --store STORE         directory that holds troubleshooting sessions
                        (default: $FIXFIRST_STORE, else .fixfirst; for mcp,
                        ~/.fixfirst/sessions)
